 of each other.\n3. **Homoscedasticity**: The variance of the residuals should be constant across all levels of the independent variable(s).\n4. **Normality of Errors**: The residuals should be normally distributed, particularly for small sample sizes.\n\nViolating these assumptions can lead to misleading results. For instance, if the residuals are correlated (i.e., autocorrelation is present), the OLS estimators remain unbiased but are no longer efficient, leading to underestimated standard errors and inflated t-statistics. This can result in incorrect conclusions regarding the significance of predictors in the model.\n\nIn summary, the Durbin-Watson d statistic serves as a crucial diagnostic tool in regression analysis, enabling researchers to identify and address issues of autocorrelation in residuals. By ensuring that the assumptions of regression analysis are met, econometricians can enhance the reliability of their models and the validity of their inferential statistics.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166014, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 578, "prompt_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 970, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "prompt_filter_results": [{"prompt_index": 0, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"fil